# Absolute base URL for canonicals, sitemap, robots, OG image URLs and
# JSON-LD. Set this to wherever the site is actually served — on Vercel
# before a custom domain exists, that is the .vercel.app address. If it
# points somewhere that does not resolve, social previews break, because
# the OG image is referenced as an absolute URL.
# Falls back to Vercel's own production URL, then to https://treeinapool.com.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Copy to .env.local for development. NEVER commit real values —
# this repository is public, and these endpoints accept writes.
# In production, set the same variables in Vercel:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production → Redeploy

# Lead delivery for both enquiry paths (project + rebuild). Formspree form
# endpoint, e.g. https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
#
# IMPORTANT: turn reCAPTCHA OFF in the Formspree form's Settings tab.
# This app posts server-to-server, which Formspree treats as an AJAX
# submission and rejects with HTTP 403 while reCAPTCHA is enabled:
#   "In order to submit via AJAX, you need to set a custom key or
#    reCAPTCHA must be disabled in this form's settings page."
# There is no request shape that works around it — a captcha needs a human
# to solve it, and there isn't one on a server. Spam protection for these
# forms belongs in this app instead (honeypot + rate limiting).
FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=

# Newsletter sign-ups (footer). Same fallback behaviour, and the same
# reCAPTCHA caveat above applies to this form too.
FORMSPREE_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=

# Show placeholder testimonials / client logos in a production build.
# Leave unset (or "false") until real, permissioned proof lands in site.ts —
# placeholders always render in development regardless of this value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_PLACEHOLDER_PROOF=
